  "user": "Fine. Back to that charge — what do I do next?",
  "answer": "I can see two TechMart Online card charges in your account, but I can't tell from here which one is the purchase where the goods didn't arrive:\n\n- **TX-0401**: EUR 240.00, TechMart Online, 20 July 2026, settled\n- **TX-0402**: EUR 240.00, TechMart Online, 14 July 2026, settled\n\nThe two charges are identical in amount and merchant, so please confirm which one you mean. If you were charged twice for the same purchase, that would be a different case from goods not arriving, and the reason code would change to `duplicate_charge`.\n\nOnce you've confirmed the transaction and the reason code, here's what happens:\n\n1. I run the eligibility check for that transaction and reason code.\n2. If it's eligible, I summarise the dispute (transaction, reason code, amount EUR 240.00 unless you want a different amount) and wait for your explicit go-ahead.\n3. Only after that do I open the dispute. This can't be reversed.\n\nIf the check comes back ineligible, I'll tell you why and what your options are.\n\nWhich transaction is it, and do you want `goods_not_received` or `duplicate_charge`?",
